 because:\n- Only one B4 remains unshown.\n- The previous player explicitly performed \u201cChi B4\u201d earlier, showing they had B3 and B5 and completed the sequence \u2014 this means they likely still have the B4 melded, and thus no longer need it.\n- However, since B4 was used in a chow and hasn\u2019t been discarded again, and only one remains, playing it now carries minimal risk of being claimed (as someone would need exactly B4 to complete a pair or chow ending/starting there).\n- More importantly, **keeping B4 contributes nothing to any high-scoring pattern**. In contrast, W3 offers potential for Dragon-like terminal honors (Pung of Terminals/Honors x1), and possibly supports Outside Hand or All Simples if paired properly.\n- Additionally, W3 appears more frequently in unshown count (4) \u2014 safer to keep as it may draw later.\n- Thus, **B4 is both less useful and marginally riskier**, making it the best discard.\n\nAnswer: Play B4"}
