7 unshown:4 \u2192 all four still exist. I hold one. So three others unaccounted. None discarded in visible history. So potentially dangerous \u2014 someone may be collecting W7s.\n\nFor example, across player has [B7,B8,B9], next has [B5,B6,B7], so B7 is popular \u2014 but W7 less so. Still, W7 could be part of a flush or sequence.\n\nBut compared to W3 and T9, which are **already fully consumed**, W7 is **live** and could help an opponent.\n\nTherefore, **W7 is the most dangerous discard**.\n\nBetween W3 and T9, both are safe.\n\nBut consider scoring:\n\nIf I keep W3\u00d73 as a pung, it's a **Pung of Terminals or Honors** (W3 is not terminal \u2014 terminals are 1 and 9). W3 is simple. So not valuable.\n\nSimilarly, T9 is terminal \u2014 but I'm discarding it.\n\nBut I have no immediate win path.\n\nBest move: discard a tile that minimizes risk and doesn't break potential.\n\nBut I must discard one.\n\nSince both W3 and T9 are safe, prefer to keep T9? Why?\n\nT9 is a terminal \u2014 could be part of \"Outside Hand\" or \"All Terminals and Honors\" if someone is going for that. But I\u2019m not.\n\nFrom my perspective: I have W3\u00d73 \u2014 I can keep that as a strong pung. W7 and T9 are both weak.\n\nBut if I discard W3, I break the pung? No \u2014 I have three, discard one \u2192 I have two left, not a pung anymore.\n\nAh! Critical point: **if I discard one W3, I go from having a concealed pung (W3\u00d73) to just a pair (W3\u00d72)** \u2014 losing the ability to use it as a meld unless I draw the fourth.\n\nBut I cannot draw now \u2014 I must discard.\n\nBut later, I might draw W3? But all W3s are gone \u2014 I hold three, one was discarded and used \u2014 so no more W3s. So I can never get a fourth.\n\nTherefore, **keeping W3\u00d73 is useless** \u2014 I can never promote to kong, and if I discard one, I lose the pung.\n\nBut currently, I have the pung in hand \u2014 but I haven't declared it. It\u2019s concealed.\n\nBut for scoring, if I ever win, having a 