dated**, or I misread.\n\nList: \"W7: 4\" \u2014 but let's check total.\n\nPerhaps it's a typo.\n\nLook at W6: unshown:0. I have [W6,W6,W6] exposed, and no other W6 seen \u2014 total 3 exposed, one must be missing. But unshown:0 \u2192 ok, so last one is in hand or wall.\n\nBut I have a pung of W6 \u2014 that\u2019s three. One more exists.\n\nUnshown:0 \u2192 means no W6 unshown \u2192 but one must be \u2014 contradiction.\n\nSame issue.\n\nTherefore, **the unshown list likely includes only tiles not yet drawn or discarded, i.e., still in the wall**, not in any hand.\n\nThat makes sense in context.\n\n\"Unshown tiles\" probably means \"remaining in the wall\".\n\nBecause otherwise, numbers don't add up.\n\nFor example, W6: unshown:0 \u2014 I have a pung (3), and one more exists \u2014 where is it? Possibly in another player's hand or discarded.\n\nBut in game history, no W6 discard mentioned? Next player played W6, previous played W6 \u2014 at least two discards.\n\nNext player: Play W6, Play W6 \u2192 two W6 discards.\n\nI have three \u2192 total five? Impossible.\n\nCheck history:\n- Next player: \"Play W6\" appears once? \"Play W6\" \u2014 one time\n- Previous player: no Play W6\n- Across: Play W6? No\n- Me: no\n\nBut I have [W6,W6,W6] exposed \u2014 so three used.\n\nNext player: \"Play W6\" \u2014 one discard\n- So total 4 accounted for.\n\nUnshown:0 \u2192 consistent.\n\nSimilarly, W7: unshown:4 \u2014 but only 4 exist, and none discarded or exposed \u2014 so all 4 still in wall? But I hold one W7.\n\nImpossible.\n\nUnless I don't hold W7.\n\nMy hand: [W3:3; W7:1; T9:1] \u2014 yes.\n\nSo I hold one W7.\n\nBut if unshown means \"in the wall\", then W7:4 means 4 in wall \u2014 but I hold one \u2014 total 5.\n\nContradiction.\n\nTherefore, the only logical conclusion is that **\"Unshown tiles\" means \"number of tiles of that type that have not been revealed in any way (not in melds, not discarded)\", so including those in players' hands and the wall, minus those